The FreeTDS Project is proud to announce the availability of FreeTDS 0.52.

FreeTDS is a open re-implementation of the TDS (Tabular DataStream) Protocol 
used by Sybase and Microsoft in their database products.  Specifically, FreeTDS
allows Linux and Unix machines to act as clients to a Microsoft SQL Server, 
Sybase ASE or ASA dataserver and related products. 

FreeTDS supports a range of protocol dialects from both vendors and three
client APIs (dblib, ctlib, and ODBC).

New features in this release include:

.. Major enhancements to the ODBC driver allowing it to work with the unixODBC 
  and iODBC driver managers as well as working with PHP and Perl ODBC 
  interfaces.
.. New configuration file format for finer grained control.  The older 
  'interfaces' format is retained as a fallback for Sybase compatibility.
.. Preliminary connection pooling code.
.. Better documentation.
.. FreeTDS is now 64bit clean.
.. Added support for nullable bit types under TDS 7.0
.. Many bug fixes.

Source packages or RPMs for FreeTDS 0.52 can be obtained at iBiblio or any of 
its mirror sites:

ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/ALPHA/freetds/freetds-0.52.tgz
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/ALPHA/freetds/freetds-0.52-1.i386.rpm
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/ALPHA/freetds/freetds-devel-0.52-1.i386.rpm

For more information on the FreeTDS project or the related FreeTDS/JDBC native 
Java driver please visit http://www.freetds.org

